# sesmesh — Solvent Excluded Surface meshes for molecules
# Copyright (c) 2026 Ugo Varetto
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use sesmesh in your work, please cite the software as below and the
  methods it implements (README, "How it works and what to cite").
type: software
title: "sesmesh: Solvent Excluded Surface meshes for molecules"
abstract: >-
  Rust library and command-line tool that computes Solvent Excluded
  (Connolly) surfaces, solvent accessible surfaces and van der Waals surfaces
  of molecules from PDB, mmCIF, XYZ and PQR files as closed, oriented triangle
  meshes with vertices on the exact surface and analytic normals (OBJ, PLY,
  MSMS).
authors:
  - given-names: Ugo
    family-names: Varetto
version: 1.1.1
date-released: "2026-11-14"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/uvar-apps/sesmesh"
url: "https://uvar-apps.github.io/sesmesh/"
keywords:
  - solvent excluded surface
  - Connolly surface
  - molecular surface
  - protein structure
  - structural biology
  - computational chemistry
  - mesh generation
  - Rust
